# Quality Checklist — Video Media World

## Before generation
- [ ] Ten source photos are present and numbered in intended order.
- [ ] Presenter portrait is accessible as a reference.
- [ ] Property facts and call to action are verified.
- [ ] Ten scene purposes and Romanian lines are prepared.
- [ ] Each scene has one camera movement and its own Image Prompt + Video Prompt.
- [ ] Pilot scene has been generated and reviewed before scaling to all ten.

## For every generated scene
- [ ] Landscape 16:9.
- [ ] Presenter is visible and speaks directly to camera.
- [ ] Face, sunglasses, blue blazer and white T-shirt remain consistent.
- [ ] Lip-sync has been visually reviewed; do not infer success from the prompt alone.
- [ ] Spoken line matches the approved Romanian text.
- [ ] No unsupported property claim is spoken.
- [ ] Architecture, furniture, finishes, doors and windows remain faithful to the source.
- [ ] No invented rooms, views, fixtures, or amenities.
- [ ] Camera movement is controlled and does not warp the room.
- [ ] Actual clip duration has been checked.
- [ ] Any defect is logged and corrected before final assembly.

## Manual edit
- [ ] All ten clips are in the intended order.
- [ ] No unintended gaps or duplicate clips.
- [ ] Each final clip is no longer than 10 seconds.
- [ ] No dialogue is cut off at a trim point.
- [ ] Voice is clear and consistent.
- [ ] Music, if used, remains below dialogue.
- [ ] Transitions are restrained and consistent.
- [ ] Any on-screen price, address, or contact detail is verified separately.
- [ ] No public sharing or publishing occurred without permission.

## Export readiness
- [ ] Final timeline reviewed.
- [ ] Final duration is measured, not estimated from requested clip lengths.
- [ ] Aspect ratio is 16:9 throughout.
- [ ] Final call to action uses supplied, verified information.
- [ ] Export is confirmed by the editing application's actual result.
